{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nGeneric search can miss Terraform declarations in sibling/local modules and overstate runtime expressions. This REB-640 child supplies conservative structural evidence to plan-review T10 Pass 1 and independent Pass 2.\n\n## Scope\n\n### Optional boundary\n\nAdd `grounding-terraform = [\"python-hcl2==8.1.3\"]` to `pyproject.toml`/`uv.lock`; register the `hcl2` probe and ABSTAIN-posture `grounding_terraform` capability. Installing the extra is the only opt-in. Lean core and non-Terraform reviews neither import `hcl2` nor advertise these tools. Extend optionality CI without a core dependency/config key.\n\n### Structural index\n\nAdd `terraform_index.py` and `terraform_tools.py`. A review-batch-owned cache captures eligible files as immutable bytes, parses them in `grounding.harness.run_in_worker`, and is freed when the batch ends. Pass 2 borrows it read-only without extending its lifetime; each agent-call ledger is discarded at call end.\n\n- Scope exists when file impact names `.tf`/`.tf.json`, or the plan names Terraform/OpenTofu and the repo contains Terraform. Each affected directory is one whole module. Follow literal repo-contained local sources forward and literal in-repo reverse callers; exclude VCS data, virtualenvs, and `.terraform/`.\n- Inspect changed `.tfvars` only when directly targeted; never infer selection.\n- Reject absolute/out-of-repo sources and escaping symlinks. Enforce 64 modules, 5,000 Terraform files, 32 MiB, and the existing 60-second deadline before returning facts. Any breach/failure yields one abstention without partial facts.\n- Parse HCL with python-hcl2 `SerializationOptions(with_meta=True)`. `__start_line__`/`__end_line__` yield line ranges only—no column/byte span. Terraform JSON reports an exact line range only for an unambiguous key; otherwise location is file-level.\n\n### Operations and contracts\n\n- `lookup_declaration(address, module_path=\"\")`: variables, locals, outputs, modules, providers, managed resources, and data resources.\n- `resolve_reference(reference, from_file)`: direct module-scope traversals and declared repo-local child outputs; it may confirm a resource base, never a provider-defined attribute.\n- Both are `job=refute` probes. A static resolution returns `refuted` at T1; every non-proof returns `abstain`; neither emits `match` or asserts absence.\n- For `grounding.schema.json`, declarations use `reference.kind=\"symbol\"`, canonical Terraform address as `name`, `language=\"terraform\"`; dotted traversals use `kind=\"member\"`. Extension `terraform_kind` carries the declaration class.\n\nAdd `src/rebar/schemas/terraform_grounding_receipt.schema.json`. Each response validates evidence against `grounding.schema.json` and its receipt against this closed schema. Required receipt fields: `schema_version`, `operation`, normalized `query`, `snapshot_digest`, `module_digest`, `backend` (parser/version, analyzer/version, config digest), effective `limits`, `outcome`, generic `reason`, Terraform `reason_detail`, and `result_digest`. The last hashes canonical safe facts before attaching the receipt.\n\nWorked receipt (digests abbreviated only here):\n\n`{\"schema_version\":1,\"operation\":\"lookup_declaration\",\"query\":{\"address\":\"module.web\",\"module\":\"infra\"},\"snapshot_digest\":\"sha256:…\",\"module_digest\":\"sha256:…\",\"backend\":{\"parser\":\"python-hcl2\",\"parser_version\":\"8.1.3\",\"analyzer\":\"rebar-terraform-structural\",\"analyzer_version\":1,\"config_digest\":\"sha256:…\"},\"limits\":{\"modules\":64,\"files\":5000,\"bytes\":33554432,\"timeout_ms\":60000},\"outcome\":\"refuted\",\"reason\":null,\"reason_detail\":null,\"result_digest\":\"sha256:…\"}`\n\nClosed abstention mapping:\n\n- missing extra → `no_tool/missing_extra`; wrong parser → `version_skew/parser_version`; non-Terraform call → `unsupported_lang/not_terraform`.\n- invalid/undecodable/unreadable input → `parse_error/invalid_input|unreadable_file`; deadline → `timeout/worker_timeout`.\n- duplicate/no unique address, dynamic source/expression, computed value, provider attribute, splat/index traversal, or unknown tfvars selection → `ambiguous/<matching_detail>`.\n- absolute/out-of-repo/escaping symlink → `private_or_internal_suspected/path_outside_snapshot`.\n- module/file/byte bound → `other/module_limit|file_limit|byte_limit`; worker crash/protocol failure → `other/worker_failure`.\n\nReturn only safe structural classes, hashes, and repo-relative locations—never credentials or string/number literal payloads.\n\n### Plan-review integration\n\nInject both tools only into Terraform-scoped T10 Pass 1. A T10 finding with Terraform evidence selects agentic Pass 2 with a fresh ledger and must issue its own tool call; it receives no implicit Pass-1 answer. Add a generic per-call tool provider/finalizer to `RunnerAgentStep`, preserving static `extra_tools`.\n\nMerge concrete reads into usage as synthetic `read_file` entries. Add signed `**/*.tf` and `**/*.tf.json` membership entries so sibling additions alter freshness via stdlib-only claim-time hashing. Missing extra advertises no tools; all runtime failures return closed abstention without becoming deterministic blockers.\n\n## Positive rationale\n\nWhole-module structural evidence addresses LLM uncertainty while reusing Rebar's worker, evidence, tool, usage, and freshness seams. It adds no scanner stage or Terraform evaluation.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nRegistry/network access, remote content, `terraform-config-inspect`, prompt edits, policy scanners, and every Terraform/OpenTofu/provider or related executable.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Lean-install subprocess tests prove the extra adds exactly `python-hcl2==8.1.3`; absent-extra/non-Terraform controls neither import it nor advertise tools.\n- [ ] Index unit tests find sibling `.tf`/`.tf.json`, bounded local-child, and reverse-caller declarations; directly targeted `.tfvars` remains unselected.\n- [ ] `lookup_declaration` tests validate exact `symbol` mapping, T1 `refuted`, line range, safe facts, and receipt.\n- [ ] `resolve_reference` tests validate exact `member` mapping and local-child output; computed/provider/dynamic controls abstain.\n- [ ] Boundary tests assert every trigger's exact `reason/reason_detail`, zero partial facts, cache/ledger retirement, worker reaping, and one-below/at/above behavior for all bounds.\n- [ ] Workflow integration captures real T10 Pass-1/Pass-2 requests with distinct ledgers; non-T10/non-Terraform controls expose neither tool.\n- [ ] Signed-read-set tests observe all parsed files and both membership patterns, then add a sibling `.tf` and observe a changed freshness digest.\n- [ ] A subprocess spy proves no Terraform, OpenTofu, provider, tfparse, TFLint, Trivy, terraform-ls, terraform-docs, or other executable launches.\n- [ ] Both schemas validate their objects; `docs/grounding.md` documents signatures, outcomes/reasons, capability posture, limits, and lifecycle.\n\n## Testing\n\nTest contract card:\n\n- Authoritative contract: REB-640, `docs/grounding.md`, and both schemas.\n- Preconditions: temp repo with sibling declarations, child output, reverse caller, dynamic expressions, escaping symlink, and bound fixtures.\n- Production path: real byte capture → worker parser → response; real request construction with only model boundary faked.\n- Tiers: parser/evidence unit-contract; workflow integration; lean-install subprocess.\n- Oracles: exact outcome/reasons/reference/location/receipt, tool names, no partial facts, retired worker/cache, changed membership digest.\n- Negative controls: CloudFormation/Python plans have no tools; literal traversal resolves while nearest computed form abstains.\n- CI: `make test` plus `.github/workflows/_optionality.yml`.\n\n## Verification\n\n`env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_index.py tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_tools.py tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py tests/unit/test_core_optionality.py tests/unit/test_capabilities.py`"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788471294913827114,"uuid":"9268fc53-f438-425c-9e0a-70550d217212"}